{%- comment -%}
  Translates a section or block SETTING through the theme's language files.

  The problem it solves: a setting's value lives in templates/*.json or
  sections/*-group.json, and its Slovak lives in Translate & Adapt — store data, outside the repo,
  invisible in a diff, and impossible to preview. Measured on 9 Oct 2026, eight footer strings had
  never been written in Slovak and were showing in English on every page of /sk/.

  How it works: the English value is handleized into a key under `prefix`. If that key exists in
  locales/*.json the translation is used; if not, the setting's own value is echoed unchanged. So
  a setting Veronka edits in the theme editor keeps working — it just stops being translated until
  someone adds the key, and the English never breaks.

  This is deliberately NOT a general translation layer. It is for the handful of settings whose
  text is effectively fixed furniture (column headings, a newsletter label) rather than content.
  Real content belongs in the language files from the start, the way the product pages do.

  Accepts:
    text   (required) the setting's value
    prefix (required) locale namespace, e.g. 'walterin.footer.block.'

  Usage: {%- render 'wui-setting-text', text: block.settings.heading, prefix: 'walterin.footer.block.' -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign key = text | strip | handleize
  if key == blank
    echo text
  else
    assign full_key = prefix | append: key
    assign translated = full_key | t
    if translated contains 'Translation missing'
      echo text
    else
      echo translated
    endif
  endif
-%}
